//! `export-add` marks one definition as an export of its program.
//!
//! A caller outside gandr calls an export by its key in the export table.
//! An export takes and gives fixed-width integers, and it performs no effect.
//!
//! The mark changes no meaning of the definition.
//! A run of the program gives the same answer with the mark and without it.

/// `add` gives the wrapping sum of two words.
@[export]
def add(a : u64, b : u64) -> u64 = u64.wrapping_add a b;

/// The sum of two words that fit.
@[runs("5u64")]
def small_sum() -> u64 = add 2u64 3u64;
